        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Enantiopure C3-symmetric carboxyl-functionalized amino-acid ligand H3L (from L- or D-phenylalanine and 1,3,5-benzenetricarboxylic acid) was reacted solvothermally with LaCl3 or La(NO3)3 in a 1:3 molar ratio in DMF/EtOH/water/formic acid at 80 °C for 2 days, affording colorless hexagonal crystals of PCC-57. The L-ligand gives (Δ)12-PCC-57 and the D-ligand gives the (Λ)12 enantiomer. The crystals are stable in MeOH, THF, DCM, MeCN, and other common organic solvents.",
